---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout title="SP+: Secure Prospective" description="SP+ is an immutable, encrypted, contained, AI-first workstation for insurance agents and financial advisors.">
  <Nav />
  <main transition:name="page-card">
    <section id="sp-plus" class="record-hero sp-plus-hero">
      <div class="record-hero-grid shell">
        <div class="record-hero-index"><span>DELIVERABLE // 001</span><span>STATE // IN BUILD</span></div>
        <div class="record-hero-copy">
          <h1>SP+.</h1>
          <p class="sp-plus-manifest">Immutable. Encrypted. Contained. AI-First.</p>
          <p>
            A safer workstation for professionals trusted with other people’s financial lives.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="record-section record-section--blue">
      <div class="record-section-grid shell">
        <aside class="record-margin"><strong>WHY // 01</strong><span>The starting point</span></aside>
        <div class="record-body">
          <h2>General convenience is not a security model.</h2>
          <p>
            Most independent advisors work on off-the-shelf computers running on residential Wi-Fi,
            exposed to intrusive pop-ups, background update risk, and un-sandboxed applications. The same
            workstation handles sensitive client PII, fixed annuities, and retirement assets on infrastructure
            built for casual home browsing.
          </p>
          <p>
            SP+ changes the starting point. It is a Fedora-based immutable desktop engineered for insurance
            agents and financial advisors who need a controlled, hardened environment without hiring an IT
            department or becoming system administrators themselves.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="security" class="record-section record-section--white">
      <div class="record-section-grid shell">
        <aside class="record-margin"><strong>SECURITY // 02</strong><span>Defensible protection</span></aside>
        <div class="record-body">
          <h2>Security by design.</h2>
          <div class="offer-grid security-grid">
            <article class="offer-item">
              <span>FOUNDATION // ENCRYPTED</span>
              <strong>Encrypted from installation</strong>
              <p>Full-disk encryption is built into the setup model, protecting client files when a laptop is lost, misplaced, or stolen.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="offer-item">
              <span>FOUNDATION // IMMUTABLE</span>
              <strong>A controlled operating foundation</strong>
              <p>The core system is immutable and updated as a managed image, reducing accidental damage, configuration drift, and unauthorized background modification.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="offer-item">
              <span>FOUNDATION // CONTAINED</span>
              <strong>Containment where it matters</strong>
              <p>Applications are isolated wherever practical. If one app is compromised, containment limits the blast radius and makes lateral movement harder.</p>
            </article>
          </div>

          <aside class="reality-card">
            <span>THE REALITY CHECK</span>
            <h3>Not a magic wand. A stronger foundation.</h3>
            <p>
              SP+ is not a replacement for multi-factor authentication, secure email, offsite backups, or a
              formal compliance program. The goal is not bulletproof perfection. It is a smaller attack surface
              and a rock-solid foundation beneath the practice.
            </p>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="record-section record-section--silver">
      <div class="record-section-grid shell">
        <aside class="record-margin"><strong>WORKFLOW // 03</strong><span>Human-held</span></aside>
        <div class="record-body">
          <h2>Human-held, AI-assisted workflows.</h2>
          <p>
            Technology should not get in the way of writing business. SP+ integrates the Pi AI harness into
            the daily desktop environment and connects it to the advisor’s existing Claude or ChatGPT subscription.
          </p>

          <div class="workflow-map" aria-label="Advisor workflow through the Pi AI harness">
            <div class="workflow-source">
              <div class="workflow-node"><span>INPUT A</span><strong>Visual screenshot</strong></div>
              <div class="workflow-node"><span>INPUT B</span><strong>Text or question</strong></div>
            </div>
            <div class="workflow-line" aria-hidden="true"></div>
            <div class="workflow-node workflow-node--core"><span>CO-PILOT</span><strong>Pi AI harness</strong></div>
            <div class="workflow-line" aria-hidden="true"></div>
            <div class="workflow-node workflow-node--output"><span>OUTPUT</span><strong>Plain-English steps</strong></div>
          </div>

          <div class="offer-grid workflow-benefits">
            <article class="offer-item">
              <span>GUIDANCE // VISUAL</span>
              <strong>Show the bottleneck</strong>
              <p>Snap a screenshot when migrating email, setting up DNS, or navigating a carrier portal.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="offer-item">
              <span>GUIDANCE // DIRECT</span>
              <strong>Know what to click next</strong>
              <p>Receive step-by-step instructions in plain English and return focus to client cases.</p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="record-section record-section--blue">
      <div class="record-section-grid shell">
        <aside class="record-margin"><strong>EVIDENCE // 04</strong><span>Built from experience</span></aside>
        <div class="record-body">
          <h2>Built from experience, not theory.</h2>
          <table class="fact-table experience-table">
            <tbody>
              <tr><th scope="row">26 years in technology</th><td>Hands-on experience with operating-system architecture, system hardening, field deployment, and open-source reliability.</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">15 years in electrical and low voltage</th><td>A physical-infrastructure mindset: grounded systems built to remain reliable under consequence.</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">6 years in insurance and annuities</th><td>First-hand experience with compliance pressure, carrier portals, advisor workflows, and the reality of writing business.</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">$110M+ annuity production assisted</th><td>Designed by someone who understands the financial value of the business sitting on the advisor’s desk.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="record-section record-section--yellow">
      <div class="record-section-grid shell">
        <aside class="record-margin"><strong>METHOD // 05</strong><span>Applied</span></aside>
        <div class="record-body">
          <h2>Diagnose. Position. Shape. Transform.</h2>
          <ul class="assurance-list sp-method">
            <li><span>01</span><strong>Diagnose</strong><p>Start with the real advisor workstation, its risks, interruptions, and obligations.</p></li>
            <li><span>02</span><strong>Position</strong><p>Place security controls and AI assistance where they improve the work without taking ownership away.</p></li>
            <li><span>03</span><strong>Shape</strong><p>Turn technical friction into plain-language guidance the advisor can understand and act on.</p></li>
            <li><span>04</span><strong>Transform</strong><p>Replace the casual home-computer starting point with an operating foundation built for the practice.</p></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="access" class="record-section record-section--ink">
      <div class="record-section-grid shell">
        <aside class="record-margin"><strong>ACCESS // 06</strong><span>Partnership model</span></aside>
        <div class="record-body">
          <h2>SP+ costs nothing but the opportunity to work with us.</h2>
          <p>
            There is no software fee and no recurring subscription invoice. Access to SP+ is earned through
            a five-production-contract partnership selected by Christopher Campbell. Those contracts qualify
            the advisor for the encrypted OS image, immutable system foundation, and Pi harness integration.
          </p>
          <div class="status-strip access-strip">
            <div><span>Software license</span><strong>None</strong></div>
            <div><span>Recurring software invoice</span><strong>None</strong></div>
            <div><span>Qualification</span><strong>5 production contracts</strong></div>
          </div>
          <a class="action action--signal" href="mailto:secureprospective@gmail.com?subject=SP%2B%20five-contract%20partnership">Discuss SP+ access <span>→</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
